    A function that returns a closure builds it in a region its caller provides.
    The region of this call is in PtrCall's frame, which is reclaimed when
    PtrCall returns.
    PtrCall's results can hold the closure only through a pointer, so its
    callers provide no region to build it in (spec section 11.5). Return the
    closure itself, an interface holding it, or a struct or array holding it,
